6|B1|purpose|noun|목적|the reason for doing something|The purpose of the survey was to learn students' opinions.|설문의 목적은 학생들의 의견을 알아보는 것이었다.|main purpose|thinking
6|B2|alternative|noun|대안|a different choice or possibility|Walking is an alternative to taking a short bus ride.|짧은 거리를 버스로 가는 대신 걷는 것도 대안이다.|an alternative to|decision
6|B2|attribute|verb|~에 기인한다고 보다|to explain something as caused by another thing|The coach attributed the team's success to regular practice.|코치는 팀의 성공을 꾸준한 연습 덕분으로 보았다.|attribute A to B|cause
6|B2|bias|noun|편향|a tendency to favor one view unfairly|The survey question may contain a hidden bias.|그 설문 문항에는 숨은 편향이 있을 수 있다.|reduce bias|thinking
6|B2|capacity|noun|수용 능력|the amount something can hold or do|The theater has a capacity of two hundred people.|그 극장은 200명을 수용할 수 있다.|storage capacity|quantity
6|B2|criterion|noun|기준|a rule used for making a judgment|Cost was one criterion used to select the design.|비용은 설계를 선택할 때 사용한 한 가지 기준이었다.|selection criterion|analysis
6|B2|debate|noun|토론|a formal discussion of different opinions|The class held a debate about school lunches.|학급은 학교 급식에 관한 토론을 열었다.|public debate|argument
6|B2|empathy|noun|공감 능력|the ability to understand another person's feelings|Listening carefully can improve empathy.|주의 깊게 듣는 일은 공감 능력을 높일 수 있다.|show empathy|people
6|B2|factor|noun|요인|one of the things that affects an outcome|Sleep is an important factor in memory.|수면은 기억에 중요한 요인이다.|key factor|analysis
6|B2|infer|verb|추론하다|to reach a conclusion from clues|We can infer her feelings from the final sentence.|마지막 문장으로 그녀의 감정을 추론할 수 있다.|infer from context|reading
6|B2|justify|verb|정당화하다|to give reasons showing a decision is reasonable|Please justify your answer with a sentence from the text.|글의 문장 하나로 답을 정당화해 보아라.|justify a choice|argument
6|B2|perception|noun|인식|the way something is understood or noticed|Our perception of time changes when we are busy.|우리는 바쁠 때 시간에 대한 인식이 달라진다.|public perception|thinking
6|B2|priority|noun|우선순위|something that is more important than others|Safety should be our first priority.|안전이 우리의 최우선순위여야 한다.|top priority|decision
6|B2|rational|adjective|합리적인|based on clear reasons rather than feelings alone|She made a rational choice after comparing the evidence.|그녀는 근거를 비교한 뒤 합리적인 선택을 했다.|rational decision|thinking
6|B2|reliable|adjective|신뢰할 만한|likely to be correct or work well|A reliable source makes the argument stronger.|신뢰할 만한 자료는 주장을 더 강하게 만든다.|reliable evidence|argument
6|B2|valid|adjective|타당한|well supported by facts or reasoning|The conclusion is valid only if the assumption is true.|그 결론은 가정이 참일 때에만 타당하다.|valid reason|thinking
6|B2|verify|verb|검증하다|to check that something is true or accurate|Verify the answer by reading the passage again.|지문을 다시 읽어서 답을 검증해 보아라.|verify a claim|analysis
7|B2|acknowledge|verb|인정하다|to accept that something is true|The writer acknowledges a weakness in the plan.|글쓴이는 계획의 약점을 인정한다.|acknowledge a problem|argument
7|B2|argument|noun|주장|a set of reasons supporting a view|A strong argument needs relevant evidence.|좋은 주장은 관련 근거가 필요하다.|make an argument|argument
7|B2|assert|verb|단언하다|to state something confidently as true|The article asserts that habits can be changed.|그 글은 습관이 바뀔 수 있다고 단언한다.|assert a claim|argument
7|B2|claim|noun|주장|a statement that someone says is true|The second paragraph challenges the first claim.|두 번째 문단은 첫 번째 주장을 반박한다.|support a claim|argument
7|B2|counterargument|noun|반론|an argument opposing another claim|The final paragraph answers a counterargument.|마지막 문단은 반론에 답한다.|address a counterargument|argument
7|B2|disagree|verb|동의하지 않다|to have a different opinion|Two experts disagree about the cause of the problem.|두 전문가는 문제의 원인에 관해 의견이 다르다.|disagree with a view|argument
7|B2|evidence-based|adjective|근거에 기반한|supported by information rather than guesswork|We need an evidence-based explanation.|우리는 근거에 기반한 설명이 필요하다.|evidence-based policy|argument
7|B2|logical|adjective|논리적인|following clear rules of reasoning|Her conclusion was logical but incomplete.|그녀의 결론은 논리적이지만 불완전했다.|logical connection|argument
7|B2|objection|noun|반대 의견|a reason for disagreeing with a proposal|The student raised an objection to the new rule.|그 학생은 새 규칙에 반대 의견을 제기했다.|raise an objection|argument
7|B2|persuade|verb|설득하다|to lead someone to accept a view|Facts may persuade readers more than loud opinions.|사실은 큰 목소리의 의견보다 독자를 더 설득할 수 있다.|persuade an audience|argument
7|B2|premise|noun|전제|an idea on which an argument is based|The argument begins with a questionable premise.|그 주장은 의심스러운 전제에서 출발한다.|false premise|argument
7|B2|qualitative|adjective|질적인|describing qualities rather than numbers|The interviews provided qualitative evidence.|인터뷰는 질적인 근거를 제공했다.|qualitative research|analysis
7|B2|reasoning|noun|추론 과정|the thinking used to reach a conclusion|Explain your reasoning rather than guessing.|추측하지 말고 추론 과정을 설명해라.|clear reasoning|argument
7|B2|rebut|verb|반박하다|to answer an argument with reasons|The researcher rebutted the criticism with new data.|연구자는 새 자료로 비판을 반박했다.|rebut an argument|argument
7|B2|therefore|adverb|그러므로|for that reason or as a result|The road was closed; therefore, we took another route.|도로가 폐쇄되었으므로 우리는 다른 길로 갔다.|and therefore|logic
7|B2|thus|adverb|따라서|as a result of what has been said|The evidence was weak; thus, the claim remained uncertain.|근거가 약했으므로 주장은 여전히 불확실했다.|thus far|logic
7|B3|concede|verb|인정하다|to admit a point despite disagreement|She conceded that the proposal would cost more.|그녀는 그 제안에 더 많은 비용이 들 것임을 인정했다.|concede a point|argument
7|B3|corroborate|verb|뒷받침하다|to provide more evidence for a statement|A second experiment corroborated the first result.|두 번째 실험은 첫 결과를 뒷받침했다.|corroborate a finding|argument
7|B3|fallacy|noun|논리적 오류|a mistake in reasoning|The conclusion relies on a common fallacy.|그 결론은 흔한 논리적 오류에 기대고 있다.|logical fallacy|argument
7|B3|refute|verb|논박하다|to prove a claim wrong by argument or evidence|New records helped refute the rumor.|새 기록은 그 소문이 틀렸음을 밝히는 데 도움이 되었다.|refute a claim|argument
8|B2|analyze|verb|분석하다|to study something by examining its parts|Analyze the paragraph before choosing a title.|제목을 고르기 전에 문단을 분석해 보아라.|analyze a text|reading
8|B2|assume|verb|가정하다|to accept something as true without proof|Do not assume that every pronoun refers to the same person.|모든 대명사가 같은 사람을 가리킨다고 가정하지 마라.|assume responsibility|thinking
8|B2|background|noun|배경 정보|information that helps explain a situation|The first paragraph gives useful background.|첫 문단은 유용한 배경 정보를 제공한다.|background information|reading
8|B2|cohesion|noun|응집성|the way parts of a text connect smoothly|Repeated key words can improve cohesion.|핵심 단어의 반복은 글의 응집성을 높일 수 있다.|textual cohesion|reading
8|B2|convention|noun|관습|an accepted way of doing something|The story breaks a familiar social convention.|그 이야기는 익숙한 사회적 관습을 깬다.|social convention|culture
8|B2|distinguish|verb|구별하다|to recognize differences between things|Distinguish the author's opinion from a reported fact.|글쓴이의 의견과 전달된 사실을 구별해라.|distinguish A from B|reading
8|B2|explicit|adjective|명시적인|stated clearly and directly|The passage contains no explicit answer to that question.|그 지문에는 그 질문에 대한 명시적인 답이 없다.|explicit statement|reading
8|B2|implicit|adjective|암묵적인|suggested without being stated directly|The final paragraph contains an implicit warning.|마지막 문단에는 암묵적인 경고가 담겨 있다.|implicit meaning|reading
8|B2|interpretation|noun|해석|an explanation of what something means|Her interpretation fits all the details in the passage.|그녀의 해석은 지문의 모든 세부 사항과 들어맞는다.|reasonable interpretation|reading
8|B2|continuity|noun|연속성|the state of continuing without a break|The repeated theme gives the essay continuity.|반복되는 주제가 그 글에 연속성을 준다.|maintain continuity|reading
8|B2|reference|noun|지시 관계|a link between a word and what it points to|Understanding the reference of it is important here.|여기서 it의 지시 대상을 이해하는 일이 중요하다.|pronoun reference|reading
8|B2|signal|verb|신호를 보내다|to show that something is coming or changing|However signals a contrast between ideas.|however는 생각들 사이의 대조를 알려 준다.|signal a contrast|reading
8|B2|structure|noun|구조|the way parts are arranged together|The structure of the essay is easy to follow.|그 글의 구조는 이해하기 쉽다.|text structure|reading
8|B2|substitute|verb|대신하다|to use one thing in place of another|The writer substitutes a familiar example for a technical one.|글쓴이는 기술적인 예시 대신 익숙한 예시를 사용한다.|substitute A for B|language
8|B2|transition|noun|전환|a change from one idea or situation to another|The word meanwhile marks a transition to a different event.|meanwhile라는 단어는 다른 사건으로 전환됨을 나타낸다.|smooth transition|reading
8|B2|unify|verb|통일하다|to make separate parts work as a whole|The repeated image helps unify the story.|반복되는 이미지는 이야기를 하나로 묶는 데 도움을 준다.|unify the text|reading
8|B3|ambiguously|adverb|모호하게|in a way that allows different meanings|The final sentence was phrased ambiguously.|마지막 문장은 모호하게 표현되었다.|speak ambiguously|language
8|B3|inference|noun|추론|a conclusion reached from clues rather than direct statements|That inference is possible, but the text gives little support.|그 추론은 가능하지만 글에서 뒷받침이 부족하다.|make an inference|reading
8|B3|subtext|noun|숨은 뜻|a meaning suggested beneath the stated words|The dialogue has a subtext of disappointment.|그 대화에는 실망이라는 숨은 뜻이 담겨 있다.|read the subtext|reading
8|B3|underlying|adjective|근본적인|lying beneath the surface of a situation|The story explores an underlying fear of change.|그 이야기는 변화에 대한 근본적인 두려움을 탐구한다.|underlying cause|reading
9|B2|central|adjective|핵심적인|most important in a particular situation|The central issue is how to reduce food waste.|핵심 문제는 음식물 쓰레기를 줄이는 방법이다.|central idea|reading
9|B2|concept|noun|개념|an abstract idea used to understand something|The article explains a difficult scientific concept.|그 글은 어려운 과학 개념을 설명한다.|basic concept|reading
9|B2|conclusion|noun|결론|a final judgment based on reasoning|The conclusion restates the writer's main point.|결론은 글쓴이의 핵심 요점을 다시 말한다.|reach a conclusion|reading
9|B2|essential|adjective|필수적인|necessary for something to work or succeed|Clean water is essential for good health.|깨끗한 물은 건강에 필수적이다.|essential information|reading
9|B2|highlight|verb|강조하다|to draw attention to what matters most|The example highlights a weakness in the policy.|그 예시는 정책의 약점을 부각한다.|highlight a problem|reading
9|B2|issue|noun|쟁점|an important topic that people discuss|The article raises an issue about online privacy.|그 글은 온라인 개인정보 보호에 관한 쟁점을 제기한다.|address an issue|reading
9|B2|major|adjective|주요한|important or large in degree|Transport is a major source of air pollution in some cities.|어떤 도시에서는 교통이 대기 오염의 주요 원인이다.|major factor|reading
9|B2|outline|verb|개요를 설명하다|to give the main points without every detail|The opening paragraph outlines the problem.|첫 문단은 문제의 개요를 설명한다.|outline a plan|reading
9|B2|overall|adjective|전반적인|considering everything together|The overall message is more hopeful than the title suggests.|전체 메시지는 제목이 암시하는 것보다 희망적이다.|overall effect|reading
9|B2|summarize|verb|요약하다|to state the main points briefly|Summarize the article in two sentences.|그 글을 두 문장으로 요약해 보아라.|summarize a passage|reading
9|B2|theme|noun|주제|a main subject developed in a text|Responsibility is a recurring theme in the story.|책임은 그 이야기에서 반복되는 주제다.|main theme|reading
9|B2|viewpoint|noun|관점|a particular way of thinking about something|The essay presents the issue from a student's viewpoint.|그 수필은 학생의 관점에서 그 문제를 제시한다.|different viewpoint|reading
9|B3|abstract|adjective|추상적인|concerned with ideas rather than physical objects|The text begins with an abstract idea and then gives examples.|그 글은 추상적인 생각으로 시작해 예시를 제시한다.|abstract concept|reading
9|B3|articulate|verb|분명히 표현하다|to explain an idea clearly in words|She articulated the problem in one sentence.|그녀는 문제를 한 문장으로 분명히 표현했다.|articulate a position|communication
9|B3|conventional|adjective|관습적인|following what is traditionally accepted|The author questions a conventional view of success.|글쓴이는 성공에 관한 관습적인 견해에 의문을 제기한다.|conventional wisdom|thinking
9|B3|elaborate|verb|상세히 설명하다|to add details to make an idea clearer|The writer elaborates on the argument in the next paragraph.|글쓴이는 다음 문단에서 주장을 상세히 설명한다.|elaborate on an idea|reading
9|B3|fundamental|adjective|근본적인|forming the basic part of something|Trust is fundamental to cooperation.|신뢰는 협력의 근본 요소다.|fundamental principle|thinking
9|B3|integrate|verb|통합하다|to combine parts into a working whole|The essay integrates several different perspectives.|그 글은 서로 다른 여러 관점을 통합한다.|integrate information|reading
9|B3|overarching|adjective|전반을 아우르는|including or influencing all parts of something|The overarching theme is the value of patience.|전체를 아우르는 주제는 인내의 가치다.|overarching goal|reading
9|B3|synthesize|verb|종합하다|to combine different ideas to form a new understanding|The final task asks students to synthesize evidence from both texts.|마지막 과제는 두 글의 근거를 종합하도록 요구한다.|synthesize evidence|analysis
10|B2|allocate|verb|배분하다|to distribute resources for particular uses|The school allocated more time to reading activities.|학교는 독서 활동에 더 많은 시간을 배분했다.|allocate resources|decision
10|B2|appropriate|adjective|적절한|suitable for a particular situation|Choose an appropriate connector for the blank.|빈칸에 적절한 연결어를 골라라.|appropriate response|reading
10|B2|contradict|verb|모순되다|to say the opposite of another statement|The new evidence contradicts the earlier explanation.|새 근거는 앞선 설명과 모순된다.|contradict a claim|logic
10|B2|correspond|verb|일치하다|to match or be related closely to something|The numbers correspond to the labels on the chart.|숫자는 그래프의 표기와 일치한다.|correspond to a pattern|logic
10|B2|eliminate|verb|제거하다|to remove something from consideration|Eliminate choices that conflict with the passage.|지문과 충돌하는 선택지를 제거해라.|eliminate an option|reading
10|B3|coincide|verb|일치하다|to happen at the same time or match|The change in weather coincided with the festival.|날씨 변화는 축제 시기와 겹쳤다.|coincide with|logic
10|B3|compelling|adjective|설득력 있는|strong enough to hold attention or convince someone|The report gives a compelling reason for change.|그 보고서는 변화를 위한 설득력 있는 이유를 제시한다.|compelling evidence|argument
10|B3|constrain|verb|제약하다|to limit possible actions or choices|Limited space constrained the design.|좁은 공간이 설계를 제약했다.|constrain a choice|decision
10|B3|contrary|adjective|반대의|different from or opposed to something|The result was contrary to our expectations.|결과는 우리의 예상과 반대였다.|contrary to expectations|logic
10|B3|deduce|verb|연역하다|to reach a conclusion using known facts|From these facts, we can deduce that the door was already open.|이 사실들로 문이 이미 열려 있었다고 연역할 수 있다.|deduce from evidence|logic
10|B3|deliberate|adjective|의도적인|done consciously and with purpose|The repeated phrase is a deliberate choice by the writer.|반복된 표현은 글쓴이의 의도적인 선택이다.|deliberate action|writing
10|B3|deviation|noun|편차|a difference from an expected course or pattern|The results showed a small deviation from the forecast.|결과는 예측에서 작은 편차를 보였다.|standard deviation|data
10|B3|dilemma|noun|딜레마|a situation involving two difficult choices|The town faced a dilemma between cost and safety.|그 마을은 비용과 안전 사이에서 딜레마에 직면했다.|face a dilemma|decision
10|B3|extrapolate|verb|외삽하다|to estimate beyond known information|We should not extrapolate too much from one small survey.|작은 설문 하나에서 지나치게 외삽해서는 안 된다.|extrapolate a trend|analysis
10|B3|hypothesis|noun|가설|an idea that can be tested with evidence|The experiment was designed to test a hypothesis.|그 실험은 가설을 검증하도록 설계되었다.|test a hypothesis|science
10|B3|inevitable|adjective|불가피한|certain to happen and hard to prevent|Some change was inevitable after the new rule was introduced.|새 규칙 도입 후 어느 정도 변화는 불가피했다.|inevitable result|cause
10|B3|inhibit|verb|억제하다|to make something slower or less likely|Poor lighting can inhibit plant growth.|조명이 부족하면 식물의 성장을 억제할 수 있다.|inhibit growth|cause
10|B3|irrelevant|adjective|관련 없는|not connected to the matter being discussed|The second example is irrelevant to the main claim.|두 번째 예시는 핵심 주장과 관련이 없다.|irrelevant detail|reading
10|B3|plausible|adjective|그럴듯한|appearing reasonable or likely to be true|The first answer sounds plausible but lacks evidence.|첫 번째 답은 그럴듯하지만 근거가 없다.|plausible explanation|logic
10|B3|tentative|adjective|잠정적인|not final and open to change|The team reached a tentative conclusion.|팀은 잠정적인 결론에 도달했다.|tentative agreement|decision
11|B3|adverse|adjective|불리한|harmful or unfavorable|The policy may have adverse effects on small stores.|그 정책은 작은 가게에 불리한 영향을 줄 수 있다.|adverse effect|policy
11|B3|aggregate|adjective|총합의|formed by adding several parts together|Aggregate demand was higher than the forecast.|총수요는 예측보다 높았다.|aggregate data|data
11|B3|autonomous|adjective|자율적인|able to act without direct control|The robot can make some autonomous decisions.|그 로봇은 일부 결정을 자율적으로 내릴 수 있다.|autonomous system|technology
11|B3|cognitive|adjective|인지의|related to thinking and learning|The task places a high cognitive demand on students.|그 과제는 학생에게 높은 인지적 부담을 준다.|cognitive load|learning
11|B3|comprehensive|adjective|포괄적인|including all or nearly all important parts|The report gives a comprehensive review of the issue.|그 보고서는 해당 쟁점을 포괄적으로 검토한다.|comprehensive analysis|analysis
11|B3|contingent|adjective|~에 달린|depending on something else happening|The project's success is contingent on public support.|프로젝트의 성공은 대중의 지지에 달려 있다.|contingent on|condition
11|B3|credible|adjective|믿을 만한|likely to be accepted as true|The witness gave a credible explanation.|증인은 믿을 만한 설명을 했다.|credible source|argument
11|B3|disparity|noun|격차|a noticeable difference between groups or amounts|The study found a disparity in access to libraries.|연구는 도서관 접근성의 격차를 발견했다.|income disparity|society
11|B3|empirical|adjective|경험적·실증적인|based on observation or experiments|The theory requires empirical support.|그 이론은 실증적 뒷받침이 필요하다.|empirical evidence|science
11|B3|equitable|adjective|공평한|fair to people with different needs|The city wanted an equitable way to share resources.|그 도시는 자원을 공평하게 나누는 방법을 원했다.|equitable access|society
11|B3|feasible|adjective|실현 가능한|possible to do with available resources|The cheaper plan is more feasible for a small school.|더 저렴한 계획이 작은 학교에는 실현 가능성이 높다.|feasible solution|decision
11|B3|heterogeneous|adjective|이질적인|consisting of different kinds or types|The group had heterogeneous learning needs.|그 집단은 서로 다른 학습 요구를 갖고 있었다.|heterogeneous population|society
11|B3|incentive|noun|유인책|something that encourages a particular action|A small reward acted as an incentive to participate.|작은 보상이 참여를 장려하는 유인책이 되었다.|provide an incentive|behavior
11|B3|infrastructure|noun|기반 시설|the basic systems a place needs to function|Reliable internet is part of modern school infrastructure.|안정적인 인터넷은 현대 학교의 기반 시설 중 하나다.|public infrastructure|technology
11|B3|interdependence|noun|상호의존|a situation in which parts rely on one another|The ecosystem shows interdependence among species.|생태계는 종 사이의 상호의존성을 보여 준다.|economic interdependence|science
11|B3|mitigate|verb|완화하다|to make a harmful effect less severe|Shade trees can mitigate heat in crowded streets.|그늘나무는 혼잡한 거리의 더위를 완화할 수 있다.|mitigate risk|policy
11|B3|resilience|noun|회복력|the ability to recover after difficulty|The town showed resilience after the flood.|그 마을은 홍수 이후 회복력을 보였다.|build resilience|society
11|B3|scarcity|noun|희소성|a situation of not having enough of something|Water scarcity shapes decisions in dry regions.|물 부족은 건조 지역의 의사결정에 영향을 준다.|resource scarcity|economics
11|B3|trade-off|noun|상충 관계|a balance in which gaining one benefit means losing another|There is a trade-off between speed and accuracy.|속도와 정확도 사이에는 상충 관계가 있다.|make a trade-off|decision
11|B3|viable|adjective|실행 가능한|capable of working successfully|The project is viable only with enough volunteers.|그 프로젝트는 충분한 자원봉사자가 있을 때만 실행 가능하다.|viable option|decision
12|B3|accountability|noun|책임성|the obligation to explain and accept responsibility for actions|Clear records increase accountability in a team.|명확한 기록은 팀의 책임성을 높인다.|public accountability|society
12|B3|adaptive|adjective|적응적인|able to change in response to conditions|An adaptive plan changes when new information appears.|적응적인 계획은 새 정보가 생기면 달라진다.|adaptive system|technology
12|B3|causal|adjective|인과적인|relating to one event producing another|A causal claim requires more than a simple correlation.|인과적 주장은 단순한 상관관계 이상의 근거가 필요하다.|causal relationship|science
12|B3|compromise|noun|타협|an agreement in which each side gives up something|The committee reached a compromise after a long debate.|위원회는 긴 토론 끝에 타협에 도달했다.|reach a compromise|society
12|B3|counterintuitive|adjective|직관에 반하는|different from what people normally expect|The study produced a counterintuitive result.|그 연구는 직관에 반하는 결과를 낳았다.|counterintuitive finding|thinking
12|B3|cumulative|adjective|누적되는|increasing as more amounts are added over time|The cumulative effect of small habits can be large.|작은 습관의 누적 효과는 클 수 있다.|cumulative impact|change
12|B3|deteriorate|verb|악화되다|to become worse over time|Road conditions may deteriorate after heavy rain.|폭우 후 도로 상태는 악화될 수 있다.|deteriorate rapidly|change
12|B3|ethical|adjective|윤리적인|related to judgments about right and wrong|The team discussed the ethical use of personal data.|팀은 개인정보의 윤리적 사용을 논의했다.|ethical issue|society
12|B3|implement|verb|실행하다|to put a plan or decision into action|The city will implement the new recycling plan next year.|시는 내년에 새 재활용 계획을 실행할 것이다.|implement a policy|policy
12|B3|innovative|adjective|혁신적인|introducing useful new ideas or methods|An innovative design reduced wasted materials.|혁신적인 설계가 낭비되는 재료를 줄였다.|innovative solution|technology
12|B3|longitudinal|adjective|종단적인|following the same subjects over time|The researchers conducted a longitudinal study of reading habits.|연구진은 독서 습관에 대한 종단 연구를 수행했다.|longitudinal study|research
12|B3|marginal|adjective|미미한|small in amount or importance|The second change brought only a marginal improvement.|두 번째 변화는 아주 작은 개선만 가져왔다.|marginal benefit|evaluation
12|B3|optimize|verb|최적화하다|to make something as effective as possible|The program tries to optimize the use of limited space.|그 프로그램은 제한된 공간의 활용을 최적화하려 한다.|optimize performance|decision
12|B3|paradox|noun|역설|a situation that seems contradictory but may be true|The story presents a paradox about freedom and rules.|그 이야기는 자유와 규칙에 관한 역설을 제시한다.|apparent paradox|thinking
12|B3|pragmatic|adjective|실용적인|focused on what works in practice|They chose a pragmatic solution rather than a perfect one.|그들은 완벽한 해결책보다 실용적인 해결책을 택했다.|pragmatic approach|decision
12|B3|provisional|adjective|임시의|arranged for now but possibly changed later|The team announced a provisional schedule.|팀은 임시 일정을 발표했다.|provisional plan|time
12|B3|replicate|verb|재현하다|to repeat a study or result to check it|Other researchers tried to replicate the experiment.|다른 연구자들은 실험을 재현하려 했다.|replicate a result|science
12|B3|robust|adjective|견고한|working well despite difficult conditions|A robust system continues to work when one part fails.|견고한 시스템은 한 부분이 고장 나도 계속 작동한다.|robust design|technology
12|B3|sustainable|adjective|지속 가능한|able to continue without exhausting resources|The school adopted a more sustainable lunch policy.|학교는 더 지속 가능한 급식 정책을 도입했다.|sustainable development|environment
12|B3|uncertainty|noun|불확실성|a lack of complete knowledge about what will happen|The plan must account for uncertainty in future demand.|그 계획은 미래 수요의 불확실성을 고려해야 한다.|reduce uncertainty|decision
